5.2932725,{"_":66,"type":67,"subtype":68,"geo":69},"Found with Roman-period material in a fill layer in the eastern area of the excavation, outside the municipal building, in the archaeological complex of the Ionic temple at Ortygia, Syracuse","found","discovered",[63,64],[63,64],{"_":72,"type":73,"subtype":74,"geo":17},"None; edited from the published photograph.","observed","autopsied",[],"Sicily","",{"_":79,"mainLang":80,"languages":81},"Ancient Greek","grc",[79],{"type":83,"bibl":84},"edition",[85],{"author":86,"date":87,"citedRange":88,"ptr":89,"inscriptionDate":87,"year":77},"Guzzardi","2012","173–174, fig. 16",{"target":90},"http://zotero.org/groups/382445/items/RW3TZH5H",{"type":92,"bibl":93},"discussion",[94,100],{"type":95,"n":96,"citedRange":97,"ptr":98,"year":77},"corpus","SGDI","II 2156, l. 6",{"target":99},"https://epigraphy.packhum.org/text/241664",{"n":101,"author":102,"date":105,"citedRange":106,"ptr":107,"inscriptionDate":105,"year":77},"Pape-Benseler",[103,104],"Pape","Benseler","1911","274, s.v. Θέξενος",{"target":108},"https://anemi.lib.uoc.gr/metadata/0/b/4/metadata-02-0000515.tkl",{"editor":110,"principal":113,"contributors":116,"change":131},{"_":111,"ref":112},"Jonathan Prag","#JP",{"_":114,"ref":115},"Valentina Mignosa","#VM",[117,120,124,128],{"_":111,"xml:id":118,"ref":119},"JP","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537",{"_":121,"xml:id":122,"ref":123},"James Chartrand","JCh","https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6823-0265",{"_":125,"xml:id":126,"ref":127},"Simona Stoyanova","SS","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9569",{"_":114,"xml:id":129,"ref":130},"VM","https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511",{"_":132,"when":133,"who":115},"File added and EpiDoc encoding","2026-08-04",[],[136],"Guzzardi, 2012",[138],"RW3TZH5H",[140,141,142,19,25,29,143,144,145,144,146,80],"isic020938","graffito of thexenos on a black-glaze kylix from syracuse",{"_":5},"syracusae","siracusa","sicily","ancient greek",[],{"title":149,"body":150,"divs":151,"editions":178,"images":188,"handnote":189},"ISic020938. Graffito of Thexenos on a black-glaze kylix from Syracuse","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"idionym\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">Θέξενος\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"idionym\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">ΘΕΞΕΝΟΣ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text after photograph (Guzzardi 2012, 174 fig. 16).\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Thexenos.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>Italian translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Thexenos.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The graffito preserves the personal name Θέξενος. Guzzardi compares this form with the well-attested name Θεόξενος. The name Θέξενος is listed by Pape and Benseler (1911, 274 s.v.) and is independently attested at Delphi in \u003Ca href=\"https://epigraphy.packhum.org/text/241664\" target=\"_blank\">SGDI II 2156, l. 6\u003C/a>, as Θέξενος Φιλαιτώλου. The use of Ξ for /ks/ is particularly significant for assigning the graffito to the Syracusan alphabet since contemporary Attic writing represented /ks/ with the digraph ΧΣ (see for comparison Dubois, IGDS I, no. 96). The forms of the other letters, including theta, are also compatible with the Syracusan alphabet, although they are not independently diagnostic. The palaeography therefore favours a Syracusan attribution for the inscription, despite the probable Attic manufacture of the kylix. An ownership function is plausible for an isolated personal name scratched on a drinking vessel, but it remains uncertain. Guzzardi regards the vessel as contemporary with the phase of the Ionic temple dated to c. 490–480 BCE, although it was recovered as residual material together with Roman-period finds in a fill layer east of the excavation and outside the municipal building. The same archaeological complex also preserves three signs incised on architectural blocks, recorded as \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004516\" target=\"_blank\">ISic004516\u003C/a> (sigma, or possibly mu), \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004517\" target=\"_blank\">ISic004517\u003C/a> (pi) and \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004518\" target=\"_blank\">ISic004518\u003C/a> (theta). \u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Guzzardi 2012 173–174, fig. 16 \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> II 2156, l. 6 \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Pape Benseler 1911 274, s.v. Θέξενος \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\"> Line 1 \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[152,155,158,161,164,166,169,172,175],{"id":153,"html":154},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"idionym\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">Θέξενος\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"idionym\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">ΘΕΞΕΝΟΣ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>",{"id":156,"html":157},"facsimile-images","\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>",{"id":159,"html":160},"apparatus","\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text after photograph (Guzzardi 2012, 174 fig. 16).\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>",{"id":162,"html":163},"translation","\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Thexenos.\u003C/p>  ",{"id":162,"html":165},"\u003Ch2>Italian translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Thexenos.\u003C/p>  ",{"id":167,"html":168},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The graffito preserves the personal name Θέξενος. Guzzardi compares this form with the well-attested name Θεόξενος. The name Θέξενος is listed by Pape and Benseler (1911, 274 s.v.) and is independently attested at Delphi in \u003Ca href=\"https://epigraphy.packhum.org/text/241664\" target=\"_blank\">SGDI II 2156, l. 6\u003C/a>, as Θέξενος Φιλαιτώλου. The use of Ξ for /ks/ is particularly significant for assigning the graffito to the Syracusan alphabet since contemporary Attic writing represented /ks/ with the digraph ΧΣ (see for comparison Dubois, IGDS I, no. 96). The forms of the other letters, including theta, are also compatible with the Syracusan alphabet, although they are not independently diagnostic. The palaeography therefore favours a Syracusan attribution for the inscription, despite the probable Attic manufacture of the kylix. An ownership function is plausible for an isolated personal name scratched on a drinking vessel, but it remains uncertain. Guzzardi regards the vessel as contemporary with the phase of the Ionic temple dated to c. 490–480 BCE, although it was recovered as residual material together with Roman-period finds in a fill layer east of the excavation and outside the municipal building. The same archaeological complex also preserves three signs incised on architectural blocks, recorded as \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004516\" target=\"_blank\">ISic004516\u003C/a> (sigma, or possibly mu), \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004517\" target=\"_blank\">ISic004517\u003C/a> (pi) and \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004518\" target=\"_blank\">ISic004518\u003C/a> (theta). \u003C/p>  ",{"id":170,"html":171},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Guzzardi 2012 173–174, fig. 16 \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> II 2156, l. 6 \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Pape Benseler 1911 274, s.v. Θέξενος \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  ",{"id":173,"html":174},"handnote"," Line 1 ",{"id":176,"html":177},"license"," Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. ",[179,181,184,185],{"html":180},"Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa",{"id":182,"lang":80,"html":183},"edition-interpretive","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"idionym\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">Θέξενος\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"html":180},{"id":186,"lang":80,"html":187},"edition-diplomatic","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"idionym\" data-text=\"Θέξενος\">ΘΕΞΕΝΟΣ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",[],[],"\u003C?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"https://epidoc.stoa.org/schema/latest/tei-epidoc.rng\" type=\"application/xml\" schematypens=\"http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0\"?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"../schematron/ircyr-checking.sch\" schematypens=\"http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron\"?>\n\u003CTEI xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xml:lang=\"en\" xmlns:xi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude\">\n    \u003CteiHeader>\n        \u003CfileDesc>\n        